      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    import sys\n    \n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    n = int(data[0])\n    \n    cuboids = []\n    index = 1\n    for i in range(n):\n        coords = list(map(int, data[index:index+6]))\n        index += 6\n        x1, y1, z1, x2, y2, z2 = coords\n        # Ensure the coordinates are in the right order\n        cuboids.append((min(x1, x2), min(y1, y2), min(z1, z2), max(x1, x2), max(y1, y2), max(z2, z1)))\n    \n    result = []\n    \n    for i in range(n):\n        count = 0\n        x1_i, y1_i, z1_i, x2_i, y2_i, z2_i = cuboids[i]\n        \n        for j in range(n):\n            if i == j:\n                continue\n                \n            x1_j, y1_j, z1_j, x2_j, y2_j, z2_j = cuboids[j]\n            \n            # Check if they share a face\n            # Two cuboids share a face if they overlap on a plane with positive area\n            # This happens when:\n            # 1. They touch exactly at one face (difference of 0 in one dimension at boundary)\n            # 2. They have overlap in the other two dimensions (creating a positive area)\n            \n            # Check for x-faces (cuboids touch at x = x2_i = x1_j or x = x2_j = x1_i)\n            if x2_i == x1_j:  # i's right face touches j's left face\n                # Check if they overlap in y and z dimensions\n                y_overlap = max(0, min(y2_i, y2_j) - max(y1_i, y1_j))\n                z_overlap = max(0, min(z2_i, z2_j) - max(z1_i, z1_j))\n                if y_overlap > 0 and z_overlap > 0:\n                    count += 1\n            elif x2_j == x1_i:  # j's right face touches i's left face\n                # Check if they overlap in y and z dimensions\n                y_overlap = max(0, min(y2_i, y2_j) - max(y1_i, y1_j))\n                z_overlap = max(0, min(z2_i, z2_j) - max(z1_i, z1_j))\n                if y_overlap > 0 and z_overlap > 0:\n                    count += 1\n            # Check for y-faces (cuboids touch at y = y2_i = y1_j or y = y2_j = y1_i)\n            elif y2_i == y1_j:  # i's top face touches j's bottom face\n                # Check if they overlap in x and z dimensions\n                x_overlap = max(0, min(x2_i, x2_j) - max(x1_i, x1_j))\n                z_overlap = max(0, min(z2_i, z2_j) - max(z1_i, z1_j))\n                if x_overlap > 0 and z_overlap > 0:\n                    count += 1\n            elif y2_j == y1_i:  # j's top face touches i's bottom face\n                # Check if they overlap in x and z dimensions\n                x_overlap = max(0, min(x2_i, x2_j) - max(x1_i, x1_j))\n                z_overlap = max(0, min(z2_i, z2_j) - max(z1_i, z1_j))\n                if x_overlap > 0 and z_overlap > 0:\n                    count += 1\n            # Check for z-faces (cuboids touch at z = z2_i = z1_j or z = z2_j = z1_i)\n            elif z2_i == z1_j:  # i's front face touches j's back face\n                # Check if they overlap in x and y dimensions\n                x_overlap = max(0, min(x2_i, x2_j) - max(x1_i, x1_j))\n                y_overlap = max(0, min(y2_i, y2_j) - max(y1_i, y1_j))\n                if x_overlap > 0 and y_overlap > 0:\n                    count += 1\n            elif z2_j == z1_i:  # j's front face touches i's back face\n                # Check if they overlap in x and y dimensions\n                x_overlap = max(0, min(x2_i, x2_j) - max(x1_i, x1_j))\n                y_overlap = max(0, min(y2_i, y2_j) - max(y1_i, y1_j))\n                if x_overlap > 0 and y_overlap > 0:\n                    count += 1\n                    \n        result.append(count)\n    \n    for r in result:\n        print(r)\n\nsolve()\n```",
