    "global index": "LiveCodeBench_204",
    "prompt": "Generate an executable Python function generated from the given prompt. The function should take stdin as input and print the output. Simply call the function after the definition. Question:\nOn a two-dimensional plane, Takahashi is initially at point (0, 0), and his initial health is H.  M items to recover health are placed on the plane; the i-th of them is placed at (x_i,y_i).\nTakahashi will make N moves.  The i-th move is as follows.\n\n- \nLet (x,y) be his current coordinates.  He consumes a health of 1 to move to the following point, depending on S_i, the i-th character of S:\n\n- (x+1,y) if S_i is R;\n- (x-1,y) if S_i is L;\n- (x,y+1) if S_i is U;\n- (x,y-1) if S_i is D.\n\n\n- \nIf Takahashi's health has become negative, he collapses and stops moving.  Otherwise, if an item is placed at the point he has moved to, and his health is strictly less than K, then he consumes the item there to make his health K.\n\n\nDetermine if Takahashi can complete the N moves without being stunned.\n\nInput\n\nThe input is given from Standard Input in the following format:\nN M H K\nS\nx_1 y_1\n\\vdots\nx_M y_M\n\nOutput\n\nPrint Yes if he can complete the N moves without being stunned; print No otherwise.\n\nConstraints\n\n\n- 1\\leq N,M,H,K\\leq 2\\times 10^5\n- S is a string of length N consisting of R, L, U, and D.\n- |x_i|,|y_i| \\leq 2\\times 10^5\n- (x_i, y_i) are pairwise distinct.\n- All values in the input are integers, except for S.\n\nSample Input 1\n\n4 2 3 1\nRUDL\n-1 -1\n1 0\n\nSample Output 1\n\nYes\n\nInitially, Takahashi's health is 3.  We describe the moves below.\n\n- \n1-st move: S_i is R, so he moves to point (1,0).  His health reduces to 2.  Although an item is placed at point (1,0), he do not consume it because his health is no less than K=1.\n\n- \n2-nd move: S_i is U, so he moves to point (1,1).  His health reduces to 1.\n\n- \n3-rd move: S_i is D, so he moves to point (1,0).  His health reduces to 0.  An item is placed at point (1,0), and his health is less than K=1, so he consumes the item to make his health 1.\n\n- \n4-th move: S_i is L, so he moves to point (0,0).  His health reduces to 0.\n\n\nThus, he can make the 4 moves without collapsing, so Yes should be printed.  Note that the health may reach 0.\n\nSample Input 2\n\n5 2 1 5\nLDRLD\n0 0\n-1 -1\n\nSample Output 2\n\nNo\n\nInitially, Takahashi's health is 1.  We describe the moves below.\n\n- \n1-st move: S_i is L, so he moves to point (-1,0).  His health reduces to 0.\n\n- \n2-nd move: S_i is D, so he moves to point (-1,-1).  His health reduces to -1.  Now that the health is -1, he collapses and stops moving.\n\n\nThus, he will be stunned, so No should be printed.\nNote that although there is an item at his initial point (0,0), he does not consume it before the 1-st move, because items are only consumed after a move.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Here's the Python solution for the described problem. The function reads input from stdin, simulates Takahashi's movement and health changes, checks whether he can complete all N moves without collapsing (i.e., health going below 0), and prints \"Yes\" or \"No\".\n\n```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().split()\n    \n    # Parse first line\n    N = int(data[0])\n    M = int(data[1])\n    H = int(data[2])\n    K = int(data[3])\n    \n    # Movement string\n    S = data[4]\n    \n    # Item positions\n    items = set()\n    index = 5\n    for _ in range(M):\n        x = int(data[index])\n        y = int(data[index + 1])\n        items.add((x, y))\n        index += 2\n    \n    # Start position\n    x, y = 0, 0\n    health = H\n    \n    # Movement direction mapping\n    move_map = {\n        'R': (1, 0),\n        'L': (-1, 0),\n        'U': (0, 1),\n        'D': (0, -1)\n    }\n    \n    # Simulate each move\n    for move in S:\n        dx, dy = move_map[move]\n        x += dx\n        y += dy\n        \n        health -= 1  # Consume 1 health per move\n        \n        if health < 0:\n            print(\"No\")\n            return\n        \n        # If at an item location, and health < K, recover to K\n        if (x, y) in items and health < K:\n            health = K\n            # Remove the item so it's not reused\n            items.remove((x, y))\n    \n    print(\"Yes\")\n\nsolve()\n```\n\n### How it works:\n- **Input parsing**: Reads all input at once for efficiency (important for large inputs up to 2×10⁵).\n- **Simulation loop**: Processes each character in string `S` to update position and health.\n- **Health check**: After each move, if health drops below 0, immediately print `\"No\"` and exit.\n- **Item consumption**: If Takahashi lands on a cell with an item **and** his health is strictly less than `K`, he heals to `K`. The item is then removed (since items are consumed only once).\n- **Final result**: If all moves are completed without health dropping below 0, print `\"Yes\"`.\n\nThis solution efficiently handles constraints using a set for O(1) item lookup and removal, making it suitable for large inputs.",
      "success": true,
