      sum_u = sum_abs_diff(u_list)\n        sum_v = sum_abs_diff(v_list)\n        group_total = (sum_u + sum_v) // 2\n        total += group_total\n\n    print(total)\n\nmain()\n```\n\nLet’s test with samples.\n\nSample 1: expect 3 → passes.\n\nSample 2: expect 11 → passes.\n\nEdge: many points.\n\nTime: O(n log n) due to sorting.\n\nn <= 200000 → acceptable.\n\nWe'll run it.\n\nBut note: the formula `sum_abs_diff` uses `idx` from 0 to n-1.\n\nFor sorted array, it computes sum_{i<j} (a_j - a_i) = sum_k a_k (2k - n + 1)\n\nYes.\n\nSo this should be correct.\n\nLet’s write the code accordingly.\n\nOne more check: two points in group: (0,0) and (1,1)\n\n- (0,0): u=0, v=0\n- (1,1): u=2, v=0\n- group even\n\nu_list = [0,2] → sum_u = 0*(0-2+1? 2*0-2+1=-1) -> 0*(-1)=0; 2*(2*1-2+1)=2*1=2 → sum_u=2\nv_list = [0,0] → sum_v=0*(2*0-2+1)+0*(...)=0\ngroup_total = (2+0)//2=1\ndist should be max(|1-0|,|1-0|)=max(1,1)=1 → yes.\n\nGood.\n\nNow output code.\n\n\n```python\ndef main():\n    import sys\n    data = sys.stdin.read().splitlines()\n    n = int(data[0])\n    points = []\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        x, y = map(int, data[i].split())\n        points.append((x, y))\n    \n    group_even = []\n    group_odd = []\n    \n    for x, y in points:\n        if (x + y) % 2 == 0:\n            group_even.append((x, y))\n        else:\n            group_odd.append((x, y))\n    \n    total = 0\n\n    for group in (group_even, group_odd):\n        size = len(group)\n        if size < 2:\n            continue\n        u_list = [x + y for x, y in group]\n        v_list = [x - y for x, y in group]\n        u_list.sort()\n        v_list.sort()\n        \n        def sum_abs_diff(arr):\n            n_arr = len(arr)\n            s = 0\n            for i, val in enumerate(arr):\n                s += val * (2 * i - n_arr + 1)\n            return s\n        \n        sum_u = sum_abs_diff(u_list)\n        sum_v = sum_abs_diff(v_list)\n        total += (sum_u + sum_v) // 2\n\n    print(total