      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    V1, V2, V3 = map(int, sys.stdin.readline().split())\n    L = 7\n    total_vol = 3 * L**3\n    # Total union volume: V1 + V2 + V3\n    # Also: |A∪B∪C| = |A|+|B|+|C| - |A∩B| - |A∩C| - |B∩C| + |A∩B∩C|\n    # But we know:\n    # V1 = only one\n    # V2 = exactly two\n    # V3 = all three\n    # So total volume covered = V1 + V2 + V3\n    # Also, sum of individual = 3*343 = 1029\n    # Sum overcounts: \n    # Each pairwise intersection counted twice in sum, but should be subtracted once -> subtract each pairwise once\n    # Triple intersection counted 3 times in singles, 3 times in pairs (as part of two sets), then added back once\n    # Alternatively: \n    # Let S1 = sum of single volumes = 3*343 = 1029\n    # Let S2 = sum of pairwise intersections\n    # Let S3 = triple intersection = V3\n    # Then: V1 = S1 - 2*S2 + 3*S3\n    #       V2 = S2 - 3*S3\n    #       V3 = S3\n    #\n    # So: S3 = V3\n    #     S2 = V2 + 3*V3\n    #     Then V1 should equal 3*343 - 2*(V2 + 3*V3) + 3*V3 = 1029 - 2*V2 - 3*V3\n    expected_V1 = 3 * 343 - 2 * V2 - 3 * V3\n    if V1 != expected_V1:\n        print(\"No\")\n        return\n\n    # Now try to find configuration\n    # Try placing cubes at small offsets\n    for da2 in range(-7, 8):\n        for db2 in range(-7, 8):\n            for dc2 in range(-7, 8):\n                for da3 in range(-7, 8):\n                    for db3 in range(-7, 8):\n                        for dc3 in range(-7, 8):\n                            a1, b1, c1 = 0, 0, 0\n                            a2, b2, c2 = da2, db2, dc2\n                            a3, b3, c3 = da3, db3, dc3\n                            if any(abs(x) > 100 for x in [a1,b1,c1,a2,b2,c2,a3,b3,c3]):\n                                continue\n                            # Compute intersections\n                            def intersect(vol1, vol2):\n                                (a1_min, a1_max) = (vol1[0], vol1[0]+7)\n                                (b1_min, b1_max) = (vol1[1], vol1[1]+7)\n                                (c1_min, c1_max) = (vol1[2], vol1[2]+7)\n                                (a2_min, a2_max) = (vol2[0], vol2[0]+7)\n                                (b2_min, b2_max) = (vol2[1], vol2[1]+7)\n                                (c2_min, c2_max) = (vol2[2], vol2[2]+7)\n                                x_overlap = max(0, min(a1_max, a2_max) - max(a1_min, a2_min))\n                                y_overlap = max(0, min(b1_max, b2_max) - max(b1_min, b2_min))\n                                z_overlap = max(0, min(c1_max, c2_max) - max(c1_min, c2_min))\n                                return x_overlap * y_overlap * z_overlap\n                            \n                            vols = [(a1,b1,c1), (a2,b2,c2), (a3,b3,c3)]\n                            inter12 = intersect(vols[0], vols[1])\n                            inter13 = intersect(vols[0], vols[2])\n                            inter23 = intersect(vols[1], vols[2])\n                            inter123 = intersect([(max(a1,a2,a3), min(a1+7,a2+7,a3+7)),\n                                                  (max(b1,b2,b3), min(b1+7,b2+7,b3+7)),\n                                                  (max(c1,c2,c3), min(c1+7,c2+7,c3+7))])\n                            if inter123 != V3:\n                                continue\n                            # Check V2: exactly two\n                            ex_two = inter12 + inter13 + inter23 - 3 * inter123\n                            if ex_two != V2:\n                                continue\n                            # Check V1: exactly one\n                            ex_one = 3*L**3 - 2*(inter12+inter13+inter23) + 3*inter123\n                            if ex_one == V1:\n                                print(\"Yes\")\n                                print(a1, b1, c1, a2, b2, c2, a3, b3, c3)\n                                return\n    print(\"No\")\n\nsolve()\n```",
