      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef countRightTriangles(grid):\n    if not grid or not grid[0]:\n        return 0\n    \n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    \n    # Count ones in each row and column\n    row_counts = [0] * rows\n    col_counts = [0] * cols\n    \n    for i in range(rows):\n        for j in range(cols):\n            if grid[i][j] == 1:\n                row_counts[i] += 1\n                col_counts[j] += 1\n    \n    count = 0\n    \n    # For each cell that contains 1, count how many right triangles can be formed\n    # with this cell as the right angle vertex\n    for i in range(rows):\n        for j in range(cols):\n            if grid[i][j] == 1:\n                # If this cell is the right angle, we need one other 1 in the same row\n                # and one other 1 in the same column\n                if row_counts[i] > 1 and col_counts[j] > 1:\n                    # Number of ways to choose one other 1 from the same row (excluding current)\n                    # and one other 1 from the same column (excluding current)\n                    count += (row_counts[i] - 1) * (col_counts[j] - 1)\n    \n    return count\n```",
