      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef furthestDistanceFromOrigin(moves: str) -> int:\n    count_L = moves.count('L')\n    count_R = moves.count('R')\n    count_blank = moves.count('_')\n    \n    # To maximize distance, assign all '_' to the direction that already has more moves\n    # If we want to go left (negative), assign '_' to 'L'\n    # If we want to go right (positive), assign '_' to 'R'\n    # We take absolute difference between L and R, then add all blanks\n    return abs(count_L - count_R) + count_blank\n```",
