hem, in the order of visiting.\n\nSample Input 2\n\n2 2\r\nab\r\ncd\n\nSample Output 2\n\nNo\n\nSample Input 3\n\n5 7\r\nskunsek\r\nnukesnu\r\nukeseku\r\nnsnnesn\r\nuekukku\n\nSample Output 3\n\nYes",
    "prediction": "Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-Next",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef main():\n    import sys\n    from collections import deque\n    \n    data = sys.stdin.read().splitlines()\n    if not data: \n        print(\"No\")\n        return\n    \n    H, W = map(int, data[0].split())\n    grid = [list(line.strip()) for line in data[1:H+1]]\n    \n    target = \"snuke\"\n    \n    # BFS: state = (row, col, index_in_target)\n    visited = set()\n    queue = deque()\n    \n    start_char = grid[0][0]\n    if start_char == 's':\n        queue.append((0, 0, 0))\n        visited.add((0, 0, 0))\n    \n    while queue:\n        r, c, idx = queue.popleft()\n        \n        if r == H-1 and c == W-1 and idx == len(target) - 1:\n            print(\"Yes\")\n            return\n        \n        next_idx = (idx + 1) % len(target)\n        \n        for dr, dc in [(0,1), (1,0), (0,-1), (-1,0)]:\n            nr, nc = r + dr, c + dc\n            if 0 <= nr < H and 0 <= nc < W:\n                if grid[nr][nc] == target[next_idx]:\n                    state = (nr, nc, next_idx)\n                    if state not in visited:\n                        visited.add(state)\n                        queue.append(state)\n    \n    print(\"No\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
