      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    t = int(input())\n    \n    for _ in range(t):\n        s = input().strip()\n        \n        # If already abc, no swap needed\n        if s == \"abc\":\n            print(\"YES\")\n            continue\n            \n        # Try all possible swaps (there are 3 pairs: 0-1, 0-2, 1-2)\n        possible = False\n        s_list = list(s)\n        \n        # Original string is not \"abc\", try each swap\n        for i in range(3):\n            for j in range(i + 1, 3):\n                # Swap positions i and j\n                s_list[i], s_list[j] = s_list[j], s_list[i]\n                \n                # Check if it becomes \"abc\"\n                if ''.join(s_list) == \"abc\":\n                    possible = True\n                \n                # Swap back to restore original\n                s_list[i], s_list[j] = s_list[j], s_list[i]\n        \n        print(\"YES\" if possible else \"NO\")\n\nsolve()\n```",
