    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef find_prime_pairs(n):\n    if n < 4:\n        return []\n    \n    # Sieve of Eratosthenes to generate primes up to n\n    is_prime = [True] * (n + 1)\n    is_prime[0] = is_prime[1] = False\n    for i in range(2, int(n**0.5) + 1):\n        if is_prime[i]:\n            for j in range(i * i, n + 1, i):\n                is_prime[j] = False\n    \n    result = []\n    for x in range(2, n // 2 + 1):\n        y = n - x\n        if is_prime[x] and is_prime[y] and x <= y:\n            result.append([x, y])\n    return result\n```",
