      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef minimum_length_after_join(words):\n    n = len(words)\n    if n == 1:\n        return len(words[0])\n\n    # Initialize the list to store the minimum lengths\n    dp = [[0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n\n    # Fill the dp list with the join lengths\n    for i in range(n):\n        dp[i][i] = len(words[i])\n    \n    for length in range(2, n + 1):  # length of the segment\n        for i in range(n - length + 1):\n            j = i + length - 1\n            # We can join words[i] and words[j], or we can take the intermediate results\n            dp[i][j] = min(\n                dp[i][j-1] + len(words[j]) - (1 if words[j-1][-1] == words[j][0] else 0),\n                dp[i+1][j] + len(words[i]) - (1 if words[i][-1] == words[i+1][0] else 0)\n            )\n\n    return dp[0][n-1]\n```",
