    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "I'll solve this step by step.\n\n## Problem Understanding\n\n1. We have 7 points A, B, C, D, E, F, G on a straight line in that order\n2. We're given the distances between adjacent points\n3. We need to find the distance between any two given points p and q\n\n## Step-by-step Solution\n\n### Step 1: Calculate positions of each point\nLet's assign position 0 to point A, then calculate the position of each subsequent point:\n- A: 0\n- B: 0 + 3 = 3\n- C: 3 + 1 = 4\n- D: 4 + 4 = 8\n- E: 8 + 1 = 9\n- F: 9 + 5 = 14\n- G: 14 + 9 = 23\n\n### Step 2: Create a mapping of points to positions\nWe need a way to quickly look up the position of any point.\n\n### Step 3: Calculate distance between two points\nThe distance between two points is the absolute difference of their positions.\n\n### Step 4: Implement the solution\n\n```python\ndef solve():\n    # Read input\n    p, q = input().split()\n    \n    # Define positions of each point from A to G\n    positions = {\n        'A': 0,\n        'B': 3,\n        'C': 4,\n        'D': 8,\n        'E': 9,\n        'F': 14,\n        'G': 23\n    }\n    \n    # Calculate distance as absolute difference between positions\n    distance = abs(positions[p] - positions[q])\n    \n    # Print the result\n    print(distance)\n\nsolve()\n```\n\nLet me verify with the examples:\n\n**Example 1: A C**\n- Position of A: 0, Position of C: 4\n- Distance: |0 - 4| = 4 ✓\n\n**Example 2: G B**\n- Position of G: 23, Position of B: 3\n- Distance: |23 - 3| = 20 ✓\n\n**Example 3: C F**\n- Position of C: 4, Position of F: 14\n- Distance: |4 - 14| = 10 ✓\n\nThe solution works correctly for all test cases.",
