    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Looking at this problem, I need to find the minimum number of deletions to make a string k-special, where k-special means the difference between the frequencies of any two characters is at most k.\n\nMy approach:\n1. Count the frequency of each character\n2. Try different target frequency ranges and calculate deletions needed\n3. For each possible minimum frequency, find the maximum allowable frequency (min_freq + k)\n4. Calculate deletions needed to bring all characters within this range\n5. Return the minimum deletions across all possible configurations\n\n```python\ndef minimumDeletions(word, k):\n    # Count frequency of each character\n    freq = {}\n    for char in word:\n        freq[char] = freq.get(char, 0) + 1\n    \n    # Get all frequencies\n    frequencies = list(freq.values())\n    frequencies.sort()\n    \n    min_deletions = float('inf')\n    \n    # Try each possible frequency as the minimum frequency in the result\n    for min_freq in range(1, max(frequencies) + 1):\n        max_freq = min_freq + k\n        deletions = 0\n        \n        for freq_val in frequencies:\n            if freq_val < min_freq:\n                # Need to delete all occurrences of this character\n                deletions += freq_val\n            elif freq_val > max_freq:\n                # Need to delete excess occurrences\n                deletions += freq_val - max_freq\n        \n        min_deletions = min(min_deletions, deletions)\n    \n    # Also consider the case where we delete everything (edge case)\n    return min_deletions\n```",
