      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef maximum_palindromes(words):\n    def is_palindrome(s):\n        return s == s[::-1]\n    \n    n = len(words)\n    count = sum(is_palindrome(word) for word in words)\n    \n    # Create a frequency dictionary for characters\n    char_count = {}\n    for word in words:\n        for char in word:\n            if char in char_count:\n                char_count[char] += 1\n            else:\n                char_count[char] = 1\n    \n    # Check how many pairs we can make from odd counts\n    odd_count = 0\n    for count in char_count.values():\n        if count % 2 == 1:\n            odd_count += 1\n    \n    # If there are odd character counts, we can use one to form a center of palindrome\n    if odd_count > 0:\n        return count + (odd_count // 2) + 1\n    else:\n        return count + (odd_count // 2)\n```",
