      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef min_equal_sum(nums1, nums2):\n    sum1 = sum(nums1)\n    sum2 = sum(nums2)\n    zeros1 = nums1.count(0)\n    zeros2 = nums2.count(0)\n    \n    # If no zeros in either array, check if sums already equal\n    if zeros1 == 0 and zeros2 == 0:\n        return sum1 if sum1 == sum2 else -1\n    \n    # Minimum possible sums (replace zeros with 1)\n    min_sum1 = sum1 + zeros1\n    min_sum2 = sum2 + zeros2\n    \n    # If one side has no zeros but its current sum < other's minimum, impossible\n    if zeros1 == 0 and sum1 < min_sum2:\n        return -1\n    if zeros2 == 0 and sum2 < min_sum1:\n        return -1\n    \n    # Target sum must be >= max(min_sum1, min_sum2)\n    target = max(min_sum1, min_sum2)\n    \n    # Check feasibility: ensure target - sum1 >= zeros1 and target - sum2 >= zeros2\n    if target - sum1 >= zeros1 and target - sum2 >= zeros2:\n        return target\n    return -1\n```",
