      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\nimport heapq\n\ndef solve():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    it = iter(data)\n    N = int(next(it)); A = int(next(it)); B = int(next(it)); C = int(next(it))\n    \n    D = []\n    for i in range(N):\n        row = [int(next(it)) for _ in range(N)]\n        D.append(row)\n    \n    # We'll use Dijkstra's algorithm with states: (time, city, mode) where mode=0 for car, mode=1 for train\n    # Since we can only switch from car to train at a city, once we choose train we must continue with train\n    \n    # dist[city][mode] = minimum time to reach city with current transport mode\n    INF = float('inf')\n    dist = [[INF] * 2 for _ in range(N)]\n    dist[0][0] = 0  # Start at city 1 (index 0) with car\n    \n    # Priority queue: (time, city, mode)\n    pq = [(0, 0, 0)]  # (time, 0-indexed city, mode)\n    \n    while pq:\n        time, u, mode = heapq.heappop(pq)\n        \n        if time > dist[u][mode]:\n            continue\n            \n        if u == N - 1:\n            print(time)\n            return\n        \n        # Try all possible next cities v\n        for v in range(N):\n            if v == u:\n                continue\n                \n            d = D[u][v]\n            \n            # Option 1: Continue with current mode\n            if mode == 0:  # Car\n                new_time = time + d * A\n                if new_time < dist[v][0]:\n                    dist[v][0] = new_time\n                    heapq.heappush(pq, (new_time, v, 0))\n                \n                # Option 2: Switch to train at city u (if not already at destination)\n                new_time = time + d * B + C\n                if new_time < dist[v][1]:\n                    dist[v][1] = new_time\n                    heapq.heappush(pq, (new_time, v, 1))\n            else:  # Already on train\n                new_time = time + d * B + C\n                if new_time < dist[v][1]:\n                    dist[v][1] = new_time\n                    heapq.heappush(pq, (new_time, v, 1))\n    \n    # If destination wasn't reached in loop, find minimum of both modes at destination\n    ans = min(dist[N-1][0], dist[N-1][1])\n    print(int(ans))\n\nsolve()\n```",
