      "generated_answer": "We need to find the minimum cost to buy at least \\( N \\) eggs when we can buy any number of packs of size 6, 8, or 12, with given prices \\( S, M, L \\).  \n\nSince \\( N \\leq 100 \\), we can brute-force all reasonable pack combinations.  \n\nHere’s the Python solution:  \n\n```python\ndef main():\n    import sys\n\n    N, S, M, L = map(int, sys.stdin.read().split())\n\n    # Upper bound for each type: we don't need more than ceil(N/min_pack_size) + a small buffer\n    max_6 = (N + 5) // 6 + 1\n    max_8 = (N + 7) // 8 + 1\n    max_12 = (N + 11) // 12 + 1\n\n    min_cost = float('inf')\n\n    for a in range(max_6 + 1):\n        for b in range(max_8 + 1):\n            for c in range(max_12 + 1):\n                total_eggs = a * 6 + b * 8 + c * 12\n                if total_eggs >= N:\n                    cost = a * S + b * M + c * L\n                    if cost < min_cost:\n                        min_cost = cost\n\n    print(min_cost)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
