      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef lexicographically_smallest_array(nums, limit):\n    n = len(nums)\n    # Pair each number with its original index\n    indexed_nums = sorted([(num, i) for i, num in enumerate(nums)])\n    \n    # Initialize result array\n    result = [0] * n\n    \n    # Group indices that can be swapped among themselves\n    i = 0\n    while i < n:\n        # Start a new group\n        j = i\n        # Extend group while consecutive numbers have difference <= limit\n        while j + 1 < n and indexed_nums[j + 1][0] - indexed_nums[j][0] <= limit:\n            j += 1\n        \n        # Collect indices in this group and sort them\n        indices = sorted([indexed_nums[k][1] for k in range(i, j + 1)])\n        \n        # Collect values in this group and sort them (ascending)\n        values = sorted([indexed_nums[k][0] for k in range(i, j + 1)])\n        \n        # Assign sorted values to sorted indices\n        for idx, val in zip(indices, values):\n            result[idx] = val\n        \n        i = j + 1\n    \n    return result\n```",
