      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef minimumSeconds(nums):\n    from collections import defaultdict\n    \n    # Map each value to list of its indices\n    positions = defaultdict(list)\n    n = len(nums)\n    \n    for i, num in enumerate(nums):\n        positions[num].append(i)\n    \n    min_time = float('inf')\n    \n    for num in positions:\n        indices = positions[num]\n        max_gap = 0\n        \n        # Circular distance between consecutive occurrences\n        for i in range(len(indices)):\n            cur = indices[i]\n            nxt = indices[(i + 1) % len(indices)]\n            gap = (nxt - cur - 1) if nxt > cur else (nxt + n - cur - 1)\n            max_gap = max(max_gap, gap)\n        \n        # Time needed is half the max gap (rounded up)\n        time = (max_gap + 1) // 2\n        min_time = min(min_time, time)\n    \n    return min_time\n```",
