      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    import sys\n    data = sys.stdin.read().splitlines()\n    H, W, N = map(int, data[0].split())\n    T = data[1]\n    S = [list(row) for row in data[2:2+H]]\n    \n    # Directions mapping\n    dx = {'L': 0, 'R': 0, 'U': -1, 'D': 1}\n    dy = {'L': -1, 'R': 1, 'U': 0, 'D': 0}\n    \n    # Find all possible starting positions (must be land and not on perimeter)\n    possible_starts = set()\n    for i in range(1, H-1):\n        for j in range(1, W-1):\n            if S[i][j] == '.':\n                possible_starts.add((i, j))\n    \n    # For each possible start, simulate the path and check if all steps are on land\n    possible_ends = set()\n    for sx, sy in possible_starts:\n        x, y = sx, sy\n        valid = True\n        for move in T:\n            nx, ny = x + dx[move], y + dy[move]\n            if S[nx][ny] != '.':  # Sea or out of bounds\n                valid = False\n                break\n            x, y = nx, ny\n        if valid:\n            possible_ends.add((x, y))\n    \n    print(len(possible_ends))\n\nsolve()\n```",
