      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef minimumOperations(num: str) -> int:\n    n = len(num)\n    min_ops = n\n    \n    # Check all possible suffixes ending with \"00\", \"25\", \"50\", \"75\"\n    for target in [\"00\", \"25\", \"50\", \"75\"]:\n        i = n - 1\n        j = 1  # index in target (start from last char of target)\n        \n        while i >= 0:\n            if j == -1:  # found both characters\n                break\n            if num[i] == target[j]:\n                j -= 1\n            else:\n                min_ops = min(min_ops, n - i - 1 + (j + 1))  # deletions so far plus remaining needed\n            i -= 1\n        \n        if j == -1:  # successfully found the full target suffix\n            min_ops = min(min_ops, n - i - 3 + 2)  # adjust for correct count\n    \n    # Also consider reducing to \"0\"\n    if \"0\" in num:\n        min_ops = min(min_ops, n - 1)\n    \n    return min_ops\n```",
