      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    MOD = 998244353\n    \n    # Read input\n    N, M = map(int, sys.stdin.readline().split())\n    \n    # For a circle of N people with M colors where no two adjacent people have the same color:\n    # This is a classic combinatorial problem\n    \n    if N == 1:\n        result = M % MOD\n    elif M == 1:\n        result = 0 if N > 1 else 1\n    else:\n        # For circular arrangements with adjacency constraints\n        # We can use the formula: (M-1)^N + (-1)^N * (M-1)\n        # This comes from applying inclusion-exclusion principle or chromatic polynomial of a cycle graph\n        \n        # Calculate (M-1)^N mod MOD using pow with three arguments for modular exponentiation\n        part1 = pow(M - 1, N, MOD)\n        \n        # Calculate (-1)^N * (M-1) mod MOD\n        part2 = (M - 1) % MOD\n        if N % 2 == 1:  # If N is odd, (-1)^N = -1\n            part2 = (-part2) % MOD\n        \n        result = (part1 + part2) % MOD\n    \n    print(result)\n\nsolve()\n```",
