      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef minCost(nums, x):\n    n = len(nums)\n    min_costs = nums[:]  # Minimum cost to collect each chocolate type so far\n    total_cost = sum(nums)  # Cost without any operations\n    \n    # Try performing k operations for k from 1 to n-1\n    for k in range(1, n):\n        # Cost of k operations\n        operation_cost = k * x\n        \n        # Update minimum cost for each chocolate type after k rotations\n        for i in range(n):\n            # After k operations, chocolate type i moves to position (i-k) mod n\n            original_pos = (i - k) % n\n            min_costs[i] = min(min_costs[i], nums[original_pos])\n        \n        # Calculate total cost with k operations\n        collection_cost = sum(min_costs)\n        total_cost = min(total_cost, operation_cost + collection_cost)\n    \n    return total_cost\n```",
