  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9331",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An internal hash table has 5 buckets, numbered 0, 1, 2, 3, 4. Keys are integers, and the hash function h(i) = i mod 5 is used, with linear resolution of collisions (i.e., if bucket h(i) is filled, the buckets h(i) + 1, h(i) + 2, ... are tried successively with all bucket numbers computed modulo 5). If elements with keys 13, 8, 24, 10, and 3 are inserted, m that order, into an initially blank hash table, then the content of the bucket numbered 2 is\n\nOptions: \nA. 10\nB. 8\nC. 10 and 24\nD. Empty\nE. 24\nF. 3\nG. 10 and 3\nH. 3 and 8\nI. 13\nJ. 13 and 8\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We insert the keys one by one using the hash function $ h(i) = i \\mod 5 $ and linear probing:\n\n- 13: $ 13 \\mod 5 = 3 $ → goes to bucket 3  \n- 8: $ 8 \\mod 5 = 3 $ → bucket 3 full, try 4 → bucket 4 empty → goes to bucket 4  \n- 24: $ 24 \\mod 5 = 4 $ → bucket 4 full, try 0 → bucket 0 empty → goes to bucket 0  \n- 10: $ 10 \\mod 5 = 0 $ → bucket 0 full, try 1 → empty → goes to bucket 1  \n- 3: $ 3 \\mod 5 = 3 $ → buckets 3, 4, 0, 1 full → try bucket 2 → empty → goes to bucket 2\n\nThus, bucket 2 contains key 3.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
      "success": true,
