    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We are given the recurrence:\n\nT(1) = 7  \nT(n+1) = T(n) + 3n, for n ≥ 1\n\nThis is a linear recurrence where each step adds 3n. Unrolling:\n\nT(n) = T(1) + 3(1) + 3(2) + ... + 3(n−1)  \n= 7 + 3 ∑_{k=1}^{n−1} k  \n= 7 + 3·(n−1)n/2  \n= Θ(n²)\n\nSo the order of growth is Θ(n²).\n\n\\boxed{J}",
