      "generated_answer": "The maximum throughput of a pipeline is determined by the clock cycle time. Since M-7 has a shorter clock cycle (7.5 ns) than M-5 (10 ns), it can complete more instructions per second, making statement I true. However, the latency of a single instruction is the time from start to finish; M-5 takes 5 stages × 10 ns = 50 ns, while M-7 takes 7 stages × 7.5 ns = 52.5 ns, so statement II is false. Statement III is also false because while M-7 has higher throughput, actual program execution speed depends on factors like stalls and dependencies.  \n\n\\boxed{C}",
