      "generated_answer": "The given statement is a biconditional: \"The university raises tuition if, and only if, both the governor approves of it and the board of trustees recommends it.\" In a biconditional \"P if and only if Q\", the antecedent is the part following \"if\" — which, despite the structure, refers to the entire right-hand side. However, in standard logical form, the antecedent is the condition that comes after \"if\", so here, \"if the governor approves and the board recommends\" is the antecedent.\n\nThus, the antecedent is the conjunction of the governor's approval and the board's recommendation, which is not listed as a single option. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{D}",
