      "generated_answer": "We analyze consistency using the given propositions:  \n1. $ D \\equiv E $ (i.e., $ D $ and $ E $ have same truth value),  \n2. $ F \\lor D $,  \n3. $ \\neg E \\cdot \\neg F $ (i.e., $ E $ and $ F $ are both false).\n\nFrom (3): $ E = \\text{false} $, $ F = \\text{false} $.  \nThen from (1): $ D \\equiv E $ ⇒ $ D = \\text{false} $.  \nCheck (2): $ F \\lor D = \\text{false} \\lor \\text{false} = \\text{false} $ — violates (2).  \nSo assuming (3) leads to contradiction → the set is **inconsistent**.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
