    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Under the LIFO (Last-In, First-Out) method, the most recently purchased items are considered sold first, so the ending inventory consists of the oldest costs. The company has 30 widgets on hand, which would come from the earliest available inventory: the Dec 2 inventory of 6 units at $2.30 and the Jan 15 purchase (next oldest), so 24 units from Jan 15 at $2.50. The total value is (6 × $2.30) + (24 × $2.50) = $13.80 + $60 = $73.80.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
