      "generated_answer": "To find the resale value where both options are equally economical, we compare the present worth of costs for leasing vs. buying. The leasing cost is $130/month × 36 months = $4,680. For buying, we calculate the present worth of the down payment ($2,500), annual loan payments on $9,000 at 5.5% over 15 years (approx $885.55/year), fuel costs ($375/year), and solve for the resale value that makes the net present value of buying equal to $4,680, using a 5% discount rate; this results in a required resale value of approximately $4,248.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
