      "generated_answer": "Gresham's Law states that when two forms of money are in circulation and one has higher intrinsic value than the other, the \"bad\" money (with lower intrinsic value) tends to circulate more widely, while the \"good\" money (with higher intrinsic value) is hoarded or removed from circulation. This leads to the phenomenon where bad money drives out good. \n\n\\boxed{A}",
