      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is E: (i) and (iii) only. Adjusted R-squared is often considered a model selection criterion with a penalty term, fitting a broad definition of information criterion. AIC penalizes less heavily than BIC, so it typically selects at least as many parameters, making (iii) true. (ii) is false because adding a term may increase the penalty more than the improvement in fit improves, and (iv) is false because AIC is not consistent.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
