\nA. the father and the son, because the forest rangers should have had better visibility controls in place during the firefighting efforts.\nB. the father and the son, because the operator's decision to fly into the smoke was an unforeseeable event that breaks the chain of causation.\nC. the pilot's estate, because the son was following his father's instructions and therefore the father is solely responsible.\nD. the father and the son, because the pilot should have been better trained to handle low-visibility situations.\nE. the pilot's estate, because the father is vicariously liable for the tortious conduct of his child.\nF. the pilot's estate, because the father and son were directly responsible for the forest fire that led to the crash.\nG. the father and the son, because the son was only 12 years old and, therefore, cannot be deemed to have acted negligently.\nH. the pilot's estate, because the father and son failed to heed the warnings about the dry conditions.\nI. the father and the son, because the operator's reckless operation of his aircraft would be viewed as a superseding cause terminating the defendant's liability.\nJ. the pilot's estate, because the son was negligent in failing to properly extinguish the campfire.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
