      "generated_answer": "The purchase order from Rainmaking was an acceptance of Costco's offer, but Costco's order confirmation added a new term (a loading charge), which materially altered the terms and thus constituted a counteroffer. Under the mirror image rule and UCC § 2-207, such a variance prevents contract formation unless the additional term is non-material or otherwise incorporated. Since the loading charge significantly changes the price, it is a material alteration, and no contract is formed unless accepted.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
