      "generated_answer": "Let the ages of the children be: Akbar = 3, Alessandro = 4, Helene = h, and Wilfred = w. The total age of the children is given as 20, so we have:\n\n\\[ 3 + 4 + h + w = 20 \\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[ h + w = 13 \\] \n\nWe also know that Helene's age is twice the average age of the group, which is:\n\n\\[\nh = 2 \\times \\left(\\frac{3 + 4 + h + w}{4}\\right) = 2 \\times \\left(\\frac{20}{4}\\right) = 10\n\\]\n\nSubstituting \\(h = 10\\) into the equation \\(h + w = 13\\) gives:\n\n\\[\n10 + w = 13 \\implies w = 3\n\\]\n\nTherefore, Wilfred's age is \\(\\boxed{3}\\).",
