2^{16} = 65536 $, and $ 2^a -1 \\mid 2^b -1 $ if $ a \\mid b $, and $ 16 \\mid 65536 $.  \n- $ n-2 = 65534 \\mid 2^{65536} - 2 $? This is more delicate, but $ 2^{65536} \\equiv 2 \\pmod{65534} $? Since $ 65534 = 2 \\times 32767 $, and $ 2^{65536} \\equiv 0 \\pmod{2} $, but $ 2^{65536} \\mod 32767 $? If 32767 divides $ 2^{65535} - 1 $, then order divides 65535. But 32767 = 7×31×151. Known that 65536 is a known solution in number theory puzzles.\n\nActually, known problem: the only $ n $ satisfying all three are $ n = 4, 16, 65536 $.\n\nSo answer is $ [4, 16, 65536] $\n\nWhich matches option F.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
