      "generated_answer": "The product is composite for all outcomes except when it is 1 (all dice show 1) or a prime number (exactly one die shows 2, 3, or 5, and the rest show 1). There is 1 outcome for a product of 1 and 15 outcomes for a prime product, totaling 16 non-composite outcomes out of 7776. Thus, the probability of a composite product is \\(1 -is 1 - 16/7776 = 485/486, which corresponds to option J.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
