    "global index": "MMLUPro_math_7310",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The curves y = (sin x + cos x)^4 and y = (sin x - cos x)^4 intersect at x = 0. If a is the smallest positive value of x at which these curves next intersect, determine the area between these curves from x = 0 to x = a.\n\nOptions: \nA. 5\nB. 3\nC. 2\nD. 4π\nE. 3π/2\nF. 2π\nG. π/2\nH. π\nI. 4\nJ. 1\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "First, note that \\( (\\sin x + \\cos x)^4 - (\\sin x - \\cos x)^4 \\) can be simplified using the identity \\( p^4 - q^4 = (p^2 - q^2)(p^2 + q^2) \\).  \n\nHere \\( p^2 - q^2 = (\\sin x + \\cos x)^2 - (\\sin x - \\cos x)^2 = 4\\sin x \\cos x = 2\\sin 2x \\)  \nand \\( p^2 + q^2 = 2(\\sin^2 x + \\cos^2 x) = 2 \\).  \n\nThus difference = \\( (2\\sin 2x)(2) = 4\\sin 2x \\).  \n\nThe curves next intersect after \\( x=0 \\) when \\( \\sin 2x = 0 \\), i.e., \\( 2x = \\pi \\Rightarrow x = \\frac{\\pi}{2} \\) (smallest positive). So \\( a = \\pi/2 \\).  \n\nArea between them from 0 to \\( a \\):  \n\n\\[\n\\int_{0}^{\\pi/2} \\left[ (\\sin x + \\cos x)^4 - (\\sin x - \\cos x)^4 \\right] dx \n= \\int_{0}^{\\pi/2} 4\\sin 2x \\, dx\n\\]\n\\[\n= 4 \\left[ -\\frac{\\cos 2x}{2} \\right]_{0}^{\\pi/2} \n= -2 (\\cos \\pi - \\cos 0)\n\\]\n\\[\n= -2(-1 - 1) = -2(-2) = 4\n\\]\n\nSo numerical area = \\( 4 \\), which matches option I.  \n\n**Final answer:** \\(\\boxed{I}\\)",
      "success": true,
