      "generated_answer": "A Type I error occurs when we reject a true null hypothesis (false alarm), while a Type II error occurs when we fail to reject a false null hypothesis (missed detection). In the dialysis center, a Type II error (failing to detect faulty equipment) is more serious because it could endanger patients' lives. For the towel manufacturer, a Type II error (failing to detect off-size towels) leads to continued production of defective products, which is more costly than a temporary unnecessary halt (Type I error).\n\n\\boxed{A}",
