    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The equation $ 2kx^2 + 5kx + 1 = 0 $ will have equal roots when the discriminant $ D = b^2 - 4ac = 0 $. Here, $ a = 2k $, $ b = 5k $, and $ c = 1 $. So, $ D = (5k)^2 - 4(2k)(1) = 25k^2 - 8k = 0 $. Solving $ 25k^2 - 8k = 0 $, we get $ k(25k - 8) = 0 $, so $ k = 0 $ or $ k = \\frac{8}{25} $. Since $ k = 0 $ would make the quadratic degenerate, the valid solution is $ k = \\frac{8}{25} $.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
