    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We solve $|x^2 - 3| = x$. Consider two cases.  \nCase 1: $x^2 - 3 \\geq 0 \\Rightarrow x^2 - 3 = x \\Rightarrow x^2 - x - 3 = 0$. Solutions: $x = \\frac{1 \\pm \\sqrt{13}}{2}$. Only $\\frac{1 + \\sqrt{13}}{2} \\approx 2.3$ satisfies $x^2 \\geq 3$ and $x \\geq 0$.  \nCase 2: $x^2 - 3 < 0 \\Rightarrow -(x^2 - 3) = x \\Rightarrow -x^2 + 3 = x \\Rightarrow x^2 + x - 3 = 0$. Solutions: $x = \\frac{-1 \\pm \\sqrt{13}}{2}$. Only $\\frac{-1 + \\sqrt{13}}{2} \\approx 1.3$ is positive and valid.  \nRoots are approximately $2.3$ and $1.3$. Range (difference) is about $1$.  \n\n\\boxed{D}",
