    "global index": "MathQA_1395",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: if c and t are positive integers , ct + c + t can not be\n\nOptions: \nA. 5\nB. 6\nC. 7\nD. 8\nE. 9\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We are given that \\(c\\) and \\(t\\) are positive integers. Let’s write  \n\\[\nct + c + t = c t + c + t + 1 - 1 = (c+1)(t+1) - 1.\n\\]  \nLet \\(m = c+1\\), \\(n = t+1\\), with \\(m \\ge 2\\), \\(n \\ge 2\\) integers.  \n\nThen \\(ct + c + t = mn - 1\\), where \\(m, n \\ge 2\\).  \n\nCheck which of the answer choices cannot be written as \\(mn - 1\\) with integers \\(m, n \\ge 2\\):\n\n- \\(5 = mn - 1 \\implies mn = 6\\): possible \\((m,n) = (2,3)\\).\n- \\(6 = mn - 1 \\implies mn = 7\\): impossible since 7 is prime and min \\(m\\) is 2, 7 not factorable as \\(a \\times b\\) with \\(a,b \\ge 2\\).\n- \\(7 = mn - 1 \\implies mn = 8\\): possible \\((2,4)\\).\n- \\(8 = mn - 1 \\implies mn = 9\\): possible \\((3,3)\\).\n- \\(9 = mn - 1 \\implies mn = 10\\): possible \\((2,5)\\).\n\nThus \\(6\\) is impossible.\n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{B}",
