    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The sampling rate must be at least twice the bandwidth, so 6 kHz. Each sample requires 4 bits (log₂16). The total bit rate per voice signal is \\(6 \\text{ kHz} \\times 4 = 24 \\text{ kbps}\\). The channel bit rate is \\(1 \\text{ μs}\\) per bit, i.e., \\(1 \\text{ Mbps}\\). Thus, the maximum number of signals is } 1 \\text{ Mbps} / 24 \\text{ kbps} \\approx 41.67\\), but the closest feasible option among the given is 30, especially if standard telephone sampling (8 kHz) is assumed, yielding about 31 signals.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
